Cobi fork patch 0007: an app-set proxy that libVLC never connects past.

Why: iOS, tvOS and Mac Catalyst have no system proxy setting that
vlc_getProxyUrl() could read. Cobi Player routes only its own traffic through
the user's VPN or proxy via an in-process gateway on 127.0.0.1, and the
gateway takes a fresh login on every start so no other local process can use
it. The app hands libVLC "http://user:pass@127.0.0.1:port" with
vlc_darwin_SetProxyUrl(). While it is set:

- Routed (src/darwin/netconf.m): http, https and the HTTP-speaking legacy
  schemes icyx/unsv/itpc (legacy http.c) and mmsh (mmsh.c) go to the proxy;
  https as CONNECT, the others in absolute form. A dead proxy fails them.
- Refused (src/input/access.c, one check in access_New): every other scheme
  except local ones (file, fd, directory, concat, data, imem, ...). That is
  the first URL and every redirect: the http module turns ICY answers into
  icyx:// and "Pragma: features" into mmsh://, and a Location may name rtsp,
  ftp, smb, ... HLS/DASH segments come through the same place.
- FFmpeg (modules/demux/avformat/demux.c) gets an empty protocol whitelist,
  so it can't open nested inputs (an HLS playlist's segments) itself.
- The login goes to the proxy as Basic Proxy-Authorization on CONNECT
  (tunnel.c; now fails the CONNECT if it can't be added) and on every
  plain-http request (connmgr.c). connmgr.c looks the proxy up once per
  request and remembers which proxy a keep-alive connection was opened
  through, so a connection from before a proxy change is dropped, not reused:
  no request goes past a newly set proxy, and the login never reaches an
  origin. A proxy URL that can't be read fails the request.
- The login never reaches the debug log: the outgoing-request lines of
  h1conn.c, legacy http.c and mmsh.c show only the request line, and legacy
  http.c no longer logs the full proxy URL.
- A bad proxy URL (not "http://[user:pass@]host:port", e.g. an unencoded '/'
  in the login, which would change the host) is replaced by a closed port
  (http://127.0.0.1:1), never by "no proxy". Out of memory aborts rather
  than going direct.

Not upstream; the 0007 number is this fork's own sequence (upstream
harflabs/SwiftVLC has an unrelated 0007). vlc_darwin_SetProxyUrl is not in
src/libvlccore.sym: that list is shared by all platforms and has no
platform-only entries, and this fork links libVLC statically.

